Checking StyleBro's rules, xunit.analyzers' assertion rules where they are warnings or errors and the built-in rules init and migrate turn on (161 ids), changing nothing; --all checks every analyzer's and compiler fix too.
Indentation kept: src/NLog.Extensions.Logging/LayoutRenderers/MicrosoftConsoleLayoutRenderer.cs:78: '#if' decides whether these lines are an if/else (or loop) body, inside a block, or (a '#region' line) compiled at all, so each framework or configuration would indent them its own way. Their indentation is left as it is.
Held back: IDE0049: this .NET SDK's 'dotnet format' ignores the suppressor StyleBro's multi-target guard uses for IDE rules, so their fixes could write C# or APIs that another target framework or project compiling the same file doesn't have. They aren't applied here; a newer .NET SDK's 'dotnet format' applies them where the guard allows.
Multi-targeted: one 'dotnet format' run per target framework (net10.0, net462, net6.0, netstandard2.0, netstandard2.1). net8.0: no run of its own, the code compiles the same as for another framework of the same kind (the same '#if' symbols tested, files and settings). netstandard2.1: only the projects whose code compiles differently there.
Shared files: these projects compile the same files with other '#if' symbols or settings, so each group gets a run of its own (loaded together, 'dotnet format' crashes: https://github.com/dotnet/roslyn/issues/86001): NLog.Extensions.Logging | NLog.Extensions.Hosting.
